# Scenario demo-lamp-tone-idle (plan 07-07, D-23, D-05, D-22, A-16): outcome pass, exit 0. The same program,
# stub, zero graphics ROM, bound and captures as demo-lamp-tone-pass with no input line, so both
# controller ports read FF for the whole run. The program stays at the idle picture (the literal F-S1:
# no lamp lit), the PSG write log holds the six init records only and the audio is silent. The asserts are
# the hand-derived expectations of data/golden/demo-lamp-tone-idle.expect (derivation in
# docs/video/demo-lamp-tone-1-derivation.md, written before the program): the same lines in the same order
# as the committed idle block of that document, and the same as the .expect (golden-expect-drift). This is
# the control of the metamorphic judge: it differs from demo-lamp-tone-pass in the video, audio, psglog,
# input and memory digests, so the response of the pass run comes from the scripted input. It asserts
# the idle literals, not the no-key timeout of the diagnostics, and it never halts.
ivss 1
id demo-lamp-tone-idle
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub-2
content grom zero-grom
content cart lamp-tone.ivsc
capture video 0 13
capture psglog
capture audio
run-to 806568 ticks
assert halted == no
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 000D
assert mem 02F2 == 00FF
assert mem 02F3 == 0000
assert mem 02F4 == 00FF
assert mem 02F5 == 0000
assert mem 02F6 == 0000
assert mem 02F7 == 0000
assert frame 0 displayed == no
assert frame 1 displayed == yes
assert frame 12 displayed == yes
assert frame 1 hash == 269b8753dd3b8e011b3fc674e071664433ae997b5f05a8227f8569eb3a1e8e70
assert frame 6 hash == 269b8753dd3b8e011b3fc674e071664433ae997b5f05a8227f8569eb3a1e8e70
assert frame 12 hash == 269b8753dd3b8e011b3fc674e071664433ae997b5f05a8227f8569eb3a1e8e70
assert frame 6 pixel 51 35 == 1
assert frame 6 pixel 107 59 == 1
assert frame 6 pixel 50 45 == 0
assert video count == 13
assert psglog count == 6
assert psglog 0 addr=8 value=003C source=cpu-write
assert psglog 1 addr=4 value=0000 source=cpu-write
assert psglog 2 addr=5 value=0000 source=cpu-write
assert psglog 3 addr=11 value=0000 source=cpu-write
assert psglog 4 addr=12 value=0000 source=cpu-write
assert psglog 5 addr=13 value=0000 source=cpu-write
assert audio at 100000 A=0 B=0 C=0
assert audio at 400000 A=0 B=0 C=0
assert audio at 800000 A=0 B=0 C=0
